1. Overall Business Insights

The four dashboards provide a connected view of logistics operations, from delivery execution to driver performance, fleet usage, and operating costs.

The major areas requiring management attention are:

1. Delivery reliability: The reported on-time delivery rate of 44.6% suggests an opportunity to investigate delays and improve service reliability.
2. Driver productivity: Driver-level comparisons can support better workload distribution and performance monitoring.
3. Fleet efficiency: The reported 81% average utilization provides a baseline for monitoring vehicle usage and availability.
4. Cost management: Monthly fuel and maintenance analysis can help identify expenditure patterns and potential cost-saving opportunities.
5. Safety improvement: Incident monitoring can support evidence-based safety training and preventive measures.

These observations identify areas for further investigation rather than proving the causes of operational problems.
